Package: RegCompassR
Title: Multiome Regulatory Evidence and Metabolic Reaction Analysis
Version: 2.2.8
Authors@R: c(person(given = "RegCompass", family = "Developers", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "dev@example.com"))
Author: RegCompass Developers [aut, cre]
Maintainer: RegCompass Developers <dev@example.com>
Description: Integrates paired single-cell RNA and ATAC regulatory evidence
    with genome-scale metabolic reaction analysis. Stage 1 fixes
    pando_args$min_cells at 300 and uses that same value before normalization.
    Standard Pando retains a broad cell type only when its total cell count is at
    least 300. Condition Pando evaluates each condition-by-cell-type stratum
    independently and removes only strata below 300 cells. Qualifying conditions
    of the same cell type remain, and the cell type proceeds when at least two
    qualifying conditions remain. Globally zero ATAC peaks are also removed
    before subsequent analysis. Stage 1 clears stale fragment references by
    default and reuses persistent motif matches across identical region layouts.
    When two or more condition levels are available, RegCompass fits one
    condition-aware Pando design per broad cell type and uses condition-full
    outerheldout TF-by-ATAC projections as the primary regulatory penalty.
    Jointly estimable edges form an auditable common-support component; edges
    non-estimable in one or both conditions contribute projectable structural
    zeros in those conditions. A supplied single-level condition directly uses
    original Pando infer_grn with unscaled predictors and no condition
    coefficients; its active edges require adjusted P below 0.05 and absolute
    coefficient above 0.01. Condition-aware runs require Pando >= 1.6.3 with
    native condition ABI 6, worker-safe registered-symbol lookup, budgeted dense
    or sparse matrix-free target execution, exact residual validation, and exact
    dense-direct or matrix-free Schur refitting. RegCompass executes Pando's
    native numerical/allocation self-test in the main process and on up to two
    supplied BiocParallel workers before target fitting starts. Pando stops
    immediately when native registration, matrix alignment, factorization,
    finite arithmetic or residual verification fails; RegCompass does not
    provide or select an R fallback. Metacells use one independent multimodal WNN
    graph per broad cell type through SuperCell SCimplify_by_graph_group. All
    conditions within a cell type jointly determine adaptive RNA and ATAC
    modality weights, neighbours, and Walktrap clusters; condition splits parent
    membership only after clustering. Metacell RNA and ATAC counts use exact
    SuperCell membership. Small metacells are retained and marked rather than
    merged or removed. RNA latent expression uses normalized-unit empirical
    Bayes updates whose shrinkage weights are independent of library size;
    observed zeros retain continuous posterior evidence and are not
    threshold-clamped. Regulatory modifiers act on bounded RNA-support odds, GPR
    rules produce reaction expression, and each medium uses one shared union GEM
    and global FASTCORE completion. Condition-specific meta-module payloads are
    stored externally so Stage 5 receives only their merged catalogue and a
    checksummed reference. Directional LP work is split into model-by-target
    blocks with one solver thread per worker. Directional structural vmax is
    solved once per shared model and target, then reused across metacells.
    Built-in medium scenarios are restricted to formulations with direct
    published-paper provenance. Depth matching, common-depth restriction, alpha
    sensitivity, zero-support sensitivity and link-saturation propagation are
    not part of the canonical workflow.
